      "classes": "1: MATCH 1 -- Both denote the air-distribution plenum.\n2: MATCH 2 -- Both denote equipment that adds moisture to air.",
      "relationships": "1: MATCH 13 -- Having a fan expresses the same part relationship.\n2: MATCH 14 -- Having a filter expresses the same part relationship.\n3: MATCH 15 -- Having a damper expresses the same part relationship.\n4: MATCH 16 -- Having a cooling valve expresses the same part relationship.\n5: MATCH 17 -- Having a heating valve expresses the same part relationship.\n6: MATCH 18 -- Having an economizer expresses the same part relationship.\n7: MATCH 8 -- Both connect the AHU to its air temperature sensor.\n8: MATCH 21 -- Both connect the AHU to its CO2 sensor.\n9: MATCH 9 -- Both connect the AHU to its air temperature setpoint.\n10: MATCH 10 -- Both connect the AHU to its cooling temperature setpoint.\n11: MATCH 11 -- Both connect the AHU to its heating temperature setpoint.\n12: MATCH 12 -- Both connect the AHU to its temperature deadband setpoint.\n13: MATCH 6 -- Both connect the thermostat to its temperature sensor.\n14: MATCH 7 -- Both connect the thermostat to its temperature setpoint.\n15: MATCH 4 -- Both connect the space to its occupancy sensor.\n16: MATCH 5 -- Both connect the zone to its occupancy sensor.\n17: NO MATCH -- No candidate connects a terminal unit to a space.\n18: MATCH 2 -- Containing a floor expresses the building–floor part relationship.\n19: MATCH 3 -- Containing a space expresses the floor–space part relationship.\n20: MATCH 1 -- Including a zone expresses the building–zone part relationship.\n21: MATCH 22 -- Having a fan expresses the same part relationship.\n22: MATCH 19 -- Both connect the AHU to its outside-air CO2 sensor.\n23: MATCH 20 -- Both connect the AHU to its return-air CO2 sensor.",
